1:28 AM\navg-cpu: %user %nice %system %iowait %steal %idle\n0.95 0.00 0.10 0.00 0.00 98.95\nDevice: tps Blk_read/s Blk_wrtn/s Blk_read Blk_wrtn\nsda 0.00 0.00 0.00 0 0\nsda1 0.00 0.00 0.00 0 0\nsda2 0.00 0.00 0.00 0 0\nsda3 0.00 0.00 0.00 0 0\nsda5 0.00 0.00 0.00 0 0\nsda6 0.00 0.00 0.00 0 0\nsdb 0.20 0.00 3.20 0 32\nsdb1 0.20 0.00 3.20 0 32\ndm-0 0.40 0.00 3.20 0 32\ndm-1 0.00 0.00 0.00 0 0\nfd0 0.00 0.00 0.00 0 0\nTime: 03:01:38 AM\navg-cpu: %user %nice %system %iowait %steal %idle\n1.25 0.00 0.15 0.00 0.00 98.60\nDevice: tps Blk_read/s Blk_wrtn/s Blk_read Blk_wrtn\nsda 0.00 0.00 0.00 0 0\nsda1 0.00 0.00 0.00 0 0\nsda2 0.00 0.00 0.00 0 0\nsda3 0.00 0.00 0.00 0 0\nsda5 0.00 0.00 0.00 0 0\nsda6 0.00 0.00 0.00 0 0\nsdb 0.20 0.00 8.00 0 80\nsdb1 0.20 0.00 8.00 0 80\ndm-0 1.00 0.00 8.00 0 80\ndm-1 0.00 0.00 0.00 0 0\nfd0 0.00 0.00 0.00 0 0\nTime: 03:01:48 AM\navg-cpu: %user %nice %system %iowait %steal %idle\n1.75 0.00 0.40 0.00 0.00 97.85\nDevice: tps Blk_read/s Blk_wrtn/s Blk_read Blk_wrtn\nsda 0.00 0.00 0.00 0 0\nsda1 0.00 0.00 0.00 0 0\nsda2 0.00 0.00 0.00 0 0\nsda3 0.00 0.00 0.00 0 0\nsda5 0.00 0.00 0.00 0 0\nsda6 0.00 0.00 0.00 0 0\nsdb 1.70 0.00 14.40 0 144\nsdb1 1.70 0.00 14.40 0 144\ndm-0 1.80 0.00 14.40 0 144\ndm-1 0.00 0.00 0.00 0 0\nfd0 0.00 0.00 0.00 0 0\n[root@rac-1 code]#"},{"type":"html","html":"<p><strong><br>\nSearching and removing files<br>\n</strong></p>"},{"type":"quote","text":"$find . -name file_name | xargs -i rm -rf {}"},{"type":"quote","text":"Be careful when using find, and it by default traverses recursively. You should add -maxdepth 1 to make sure it doesn’t delete stuff in subfolders unless you want it to.\nIn addition, using xargs for deleting small numbers of files, but there’s a maximum number of arguments you can pass to rm, and many other programs. If you need to delete files by the thousands, use a for loop.\nfor i in /home/me/tmp/*; do rm -f $i; done\nReply With Quote"},{"type":"html","html":"<p><strong>Stat</strong></p>"},{"type":"quote","text":"[root@rac-1 code]# stat progress-ber2.sh\nFile: `progress-ber2.sh’\nSize: 482 Blocks: 8 IO Block: 4096 regular file\nDevice: fd00h/64768d Inode: 8552721 Links: 1\nAccess: (0644/-rw-r–r–) Uid: ( 0/ root) Gid: ( 0/ root)\nAccess: 2010-09-07 07:28:10.000000000 +0530\nModify: 2010-09-07 07:23:35.000000000 +0530\nChange: 2010-09-07 07:23:35.000000000 +0530\n[root@rac-1 code]# stat -f progress-ber2.sh\nFile: “progress-ber2.sh”\nID: 0 Namelen: 255 Type: ext2/ext3\nBlock size: 4096 Fundamental block size: 4096\nBlocks: Total: 43454618 Free: 36041658 Available: 33798689\nInodes: Total: 44859392 Free: 44570073\n[root@rac-1 code]#"},{"type":"html","html":"<p><strong>Top 10 file w.r.t there size: </strong></p>"},{"type":"quote","text":"find . -type f | xargs ls -s | sort -rn | awk ‘{size=$1/1024; printf(“%dMb %s\\n”, size,$2);}’ | head\nor\ndu -xak . | sort -n | awk ‘{size=$1/1024; path=””; for (i=2; i 50) { printf(“%dMb %s\\n”, size,path); } }’\nor\ndu -a /var | sort -n -r | head -n 10"},{"type":"html","html":"<p><strong>Deletion by Month</strong></p>"},{"type":"quote","text":"ls -lh | awk ‘{print $6 ” ” $9}’ | sed -n ‘/Mar/p’ | xargs rm -rf"},{"type":"paragraph","text":"Have fun"}]'::jsonb,
  NULL, 'csayantan', '{}'::text[], '{}'::text[], '{"title":"Linux for EBS R12 DBA","description":"RHEL 5.3 VNC server configuration: $vncserver Edit /home/username/.vnc/xstartup script as #!/bin/sh # Uncomment the following two lines for normal desktop…","canonical":"https://cadentic.dev/linux-rhel5-basics","noindex":false}'::jsonb, 'draft', NULL,
