SELECT gen_random_uuid(), 'page', 10, 'ebs-r12-after-fsck', 'EBS R12 after readonly filesystem or fsck adformsctl.sh : exiting with status 204', 'Had a conference with customer and found the below : Unable to start/run any “AD” scripts under $ADMIN_SCRIPTS_HOME”. For example : Unable to start the concurrent manager using adcmctl.sh script. Below error can be seen : Permission denied: Could write in “adcmctl.txt” : read only file system. We…', '{"type":"none"}'::jsonb, '[{"type":"html","html":"<p><strong><br>\nHad a conference with customer and found the below :</strong></p>"},{"type":"paragraph","text":"Unable to start/run any “AD” scripts under $ADMIN_SCRIPTS_HOME”. For example : Unable to start the concurrent manager using adcmctl.sh script. Below error can be seen :"},{"type":"paragraph","text":"Permission denied: Could write in “adcmctl.txt” : read only file system."},{"type":"paragraph","text":"We have tried to change the permission but the same “read only file system was coming”. To confirm the issue we tried to create a directory or file using “mkdir” and “touch” command respectively but got the same error. Customer has confirmed that it was 15 days back they found it working after that its not working."},{"type":"paragraph","text":"Explained to customer that the issue is not with EBS but with some other operating system related. Please check with your OS administrator and make sure that this read only file system error will not come."},{"type":"paragraph","text":"Action Plan\n================\n1.) Check with your OS administrator and resolve the “Read only file system error”. It is a OS permission error. Update the SR once it got resolved."},{"type":"quote","text":"fsck /u02\nit will ask to recover or inode entry to change and make them to change.\nlet the system to reboot."},{"type":"quote","text":"when we restarted the application we found the error.\nand found missing of OA_HTML folder on the specific location.\noafm,forms and oacore not starting up\nDOC:412980.1 resolved my issues\nadformsctl.sh : exiting with status 204\nadoafmctl.sh : exiting with status 204\nadoacorectl.sh : exiting with status 204\n- check if it is really down: ps -ef | grep grep opm for windows check if all java.exe processes are gone.\n6 - delete the following:\nrm -fr $INST_TOP/ora/10.1.3/j2ee/oacore/persistence/*\nrm -fr $INST_TOP/ora/10.1.3/j2ee/oafm/persistence/*\nrm -fr $INST_TOP/ora/10.1.3/j2ee/forms/persistence/*\n6 - execute autoconfig at the Application Tier\n$ADMIN_SCRIPTS_HOME/adautocfg.sh\n7 - start all Applications Services\nadstrtall.sh apps/\n8 - check if the issue has been resolved: adapcctl.sh status"}]'::jsonb,
  NULL, 'csayantan', '{}'::text[], '{}'::text[], '{"title":"EBS R12 after readonly filesystem or fsck adformsctl.sh : exiting with status 204","description":"Had a conference with customer and found the below : Unable to start/run any “AD” scripts under $ADMIN_SCRIPTS_HOME”. For example : Unable to start the…","canonical":"https://cadentic.dev/oracle-apps-r12/ebs-r12-after-fsck","noindex":false}'::jsonb, 'draft', NULL,
  '2010-07-22T10:50:25Z'::timestamptz, 'wordpress', '186', now(), now()
