SELECT gen_random_uuid(), 'page', 0, 'teradata', 'Teradata 12.0 / Teradata 13.0', 'Formally speaking, the difference between a user and a database is that a user has a password and a database does not. Users can also have default attributes such as time zone, date form, character set, role, and profile, while databases cannot. You might infer from this that databases are passive…', '{"type":"none"}'::jsonb, '[{"type":"paragraph","text":"Formally speaking, the difference between a user and a database is that a user has a password"},{"type":"paragraph","text":"and a database does not. Users can also have default attributes such as time zone, date form,"},{"type":"paragraph","text":"character set, role, and profile, while databases cannot. You might infer from this that"},{"type":"paragraph","text":"databases are passive objects, while users are active objects. That is only true in the sense that"},{"type":"paragraph","text":"databases cannot execute SQL statements. However, a query, macro, or stored procedure can"},{"type":"paragraph","text":"execute using the privileges of the database."},{"type":"paragraph","text":"* Teradata Has macro too."},{"type":"paragraph","text":"A day with SEL and Teradata"},{"type":"quote","text":"s10-1310:~ # pdestat\nSnapshot Statistics for all PDE subsystems:\n——————————————-\nThu Mar 22 13:28:11 2012\n————————\nsysusersleep 229 sysuserwakeup 8\nsysreadkmem 128 sysuserwakeupandsleep 0\nsysuserreasonsleep 2657 sysuserreasonwakeup 2571\nsysuserlockcreate 52 sysuserlockdestroy 0\nsysuserlocklock 87496 sysuserlockunlock 87496\nsyswritekmem 0 syssch_setpg 678\nsyssch_getpg 507 syssch_gdochange 2\nsyssch_info 0 sysukeventcreate 61\nsysukeventdestroy 4 sysukeventset 102417\nsysukeventreset 12 sysukeventwait 49799\nsysfastlockcreate 0 sysfastlockdestroy 0\nsysfastlocklock 0 sysfastlockunlock 0\nsyssch_delaytask 0 syssch_spsinfo 0\nsysevdaemon 1 sysdiag 0\ntpainit 1 tpaexit 0\ntpavprinit 7 tpavprexit 0\ntpatrace 109 tpatrace2 0\ntpanodevprid 1 tpanodecrash 0\nprgentry 35 prgexit 0\nprgadminwait 482 prgwakepart 21\nprgwakeall 0 prgwakerequestor 21\nprgproctime 0\ntskkentry 579 tskkexit 79\ntskresource_k 1489 tskinfo_k 2401\ntsksetwid 0\nGdoMap 6 GdoUnmap 0\nGdoWrite 52 GdoRead 74\ngdo_tpatrace 200 gdocallback 5\nfsgacquire 26061 fsgalter 46893\nfsgio 9235 fsgrelease 15428\nfsginquire 15775 fsginfo 22\nfsgkvinit 10 fsgkpartinit 11\nfsgresource 0 fsgstop 2\nfsgopen_ownpdisk 6 fsginputparam 0\nfsgcacheclean 0 fsgstatsctl 1\nsegaccess 6464 segaccessloc 0\nsegchange 121 segdiscard 3955\nsegdrop 2003 segexist 1715\nsegget 6127 seggetloc 0\nsegiddiscard 5 segident 203\nseglock 9 segrelocate 0\nSegInit 3 SegInitDone 1\nSegResource 4 SegInfo 0\nSegTskGetParent 382 SegTskGetChild 382\nSegFreeCount 5 segmmwaitio 0\nSegLocInfo 0 seggetlocal 0\nlogthrottle 21 lognsread 2\nlogaddtable 2 logfinderr 26\nlogsetcat 0\nmonallocate 121 mondeallocate 0\nmonenter 18037 monleave 18037\nmonresource 0 monresume 11\nmonyieldwait 15\ntdnactivate 1 tdn_tune_init 1\ntdn_tune_init_check 1 tdntune 0\ntdnrnget 0 tdnrnwait 0\ntdnfcdirtynow 0 tdnfcdirtymax 0\ntdnfcfailures 0 tdnfcunboundnow 453\ntdnfcboundnow 70 tdnfcboundmax 82\ntdnfcfreenow 32244 tdnfcfreemin 32243\ntdnfcallocs 614 tdnfcfrees 91\ntdnfcbinds 634 tdnfcunbinds 564\nnetqflushbydest 0 netqcheckbydest 37\nnetqflushvproc 0 netqcheckbysource 0\nmsgchkq 70 msgchnlink 22\nmsgchnunlnk 19 msggetbx 1213\nmsggtbxe 128 msghtran 0\nmsgnumbx 98 msgputbx 573\nmsgrxrec 1461 msgrxseg 1234\nmsgsigbx 9 msgt2rec 22\nmsgtxrec 2399 msgtxseg 1528\nmsgwrkbx 4 msgrxsegrec 1488\nmsgtxrecseg 162 msgrxrecseg 163\nmsgwrkinfo 1 msgschinfo 0\nmsgworkkill 0 msgresource 0\nmsgkchnunlnk 0 msgkevdaemon 1\nmsgkmsgtrace 3023 msgktxtrace 909\nmsgtxrecfsg 0 msgawtinfo 0\nmsgmsgreset 0 msgfindbx 0\nmsgtxall 0 msgrxall 147479\nmsgifchnlink 0 msgkerdaemon 1\nmsgawtinfolong 0 msgdebuginit 1\nmrgclear 0 mrginix 0\nmrgmove 0 mrgrowpack 0\nmrgdaemon 2\ngsmget 78 gsmput 0\ngsmdecr 60 gsmincr 64\ngsmread 8 gsmwrite 5\ngsmknownget 5 gsmpmaget 0\ngsmsub 0 gsmadd 0\ngsmatomic 0\ngrpget 8 grpput 1\ngrpenter 36 grpleave 0\ngrptest 29 grpabort 0\ngrpcount 102 grpvalid 0\ngrpinvalid 1 grpswitch 0\ngrpvmember 4 grpventer 32\ngrpcountlastenter 0\nchnget 196 chnput 186\nchnfirst 92 chnsignal 230\nchnread 10 chnstate 0\nchnset 61 chnunassign 94\nchnsigcount 0 chncount 0\nchnsiginit 1 chnsigdata 0\nchndata 0\nchnlastdone 154\nRssMap 1 RssUnMap 0\nRssKCollect 19 RssKMacroOff 0\ntrawrite 0 traread 1\ntraswitch 0 trakinit 1\ntrarestartrecord 0\nstart_tpa 0 select_coordinator 1\nselect_tpa 1 synchronize_tpa 25\ntdnreset 0 tdnresetresp 0\ntdnresetdone 0 tdnresetpart 0\ntdnresetrecv 1 block_work 1\nblock_stop 0 tdnreleasemem 0\ns10-1310:~ #"},{"type":"paragraph","text":"—- Teradata"},{"type":"paragraph","text":"Oracle Database includes a number of predefined user accounts. The three types of predefined accounts are:"},{"type":"paragraph","text":"Administrative accounts (SYS, SYSTEM, SYSMAN, and DBSNMP)"},{"type":"paragraph","text":"SYS and SYSTEM are described in “About Database Administrator Security and Privileges”. SYSMAN is used to perform Oracle Enterprise Manager administration tasks. The management agent of Enterprise Manager uses the DBSNMP account to monitor and manage the database. You must not delete these accounts."},{"type":"paragraph","text":"Sample schema accounts"},{"type":"paragraph","text":"These accounts are used for examples in Oracle Database documentation and instructional materials. Examples are HR, SH, and OE. You must unlock these accounts and reset their passwords before using them."},{"type":"paragraph","text":"Internal accounts."},{"type":"paragraph","text":"These accounts are created so that individual Oracle Database features or components can have their own schemas. You must not delete internal accounts, and you must not attempt to log in with them."},{"type":"paragraph","text":"—- Oracle"},{"type":"html","html":"<p><a href=\"http://in.linkedin.com/pub/sayantan-chakraborty/41/512/758\">View sayantan chakraborty’s profile</a></p>"},{"type":"html","html":"<figure><img src=\"https://i0.wp.com/www.linkedin.com/img/webpromo/btn_in_20x15.png\" alt=\"View sayantan chakraborty&#39;s LinkedIn profile\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>"}]'::jsonb,
  NULL, 'csayantan', '{}'::text[], '{}'::text[], '{"title":"Teradata 12.0 / Teradata 13.0","description":"Formally speaking, the difference between a user and a database is that a user has a password and a database does not. Users can also have default attributes…","canonical":"https://cadentic.dev/teradata","noindex":false}'::jsonb, 'draft', NULL,
